# `kevin rerun`

Reruns one step of a running `kevin run`, the same as the console's rerun button. It returns once the rerun finishes, prints the state of the step and of any other step that changed, and exits nonzero if the step failed. It fails if the step does not exist or is already running, and if kevin is not running for this project and environment. Interrupting the command cancels the rerun.

With `--cascade`, kevin also reruns the steps that depend on the step. A dependent that never completed always runs. A dependent that already completed runs only if its step type is idempotent.

`kevin rerun` covers `env` steps only.

```sh
kevin rerun web
kevin rerun web --cascade
```

[[template "flags" .]]

See [`kevin status`]({{< relref "/docs/reference/commands/status" >}}) for step state, and [`kevin logs`]({{< relref "/docs/reference/commands/logs" >}}) for the output of a step.
